<header><p class="eyebrow">November 12, 2026 PT · Men and women · Authenticated owner result</p><h1>The old owner exited.<br>A startup test blocked science.</h1><p class="intro">The actual B063R5 return verifies successful scoped recovery and an independent observer working on the owner. A separate test-fixture cleanup defect then stopped the new worker before scientific work began. B063R6 repairs that fixture and reduces repeated preflight work.</p></header>
<div class="cards" id="r6-cards"><div class="card"><strong>Recovered</strong><span>Old owner exit and exact lease release verified</span></div><div class="card"><strong>1</strong><span>Errored startup case<br>3 subtest cleanup errors</span></div><div class="card"><strong>0</strong><span>New scientific fits in the actual R5 attempt</span></div><div class="card"><strong>22</strong><span>Prior target fits preserved<br>134 exact objects reverified</span></div></div>
<aside class="notice" id="r6-scope"><p><strong>Recovery succeeded; scientific execution remains incomplete.</strong> The return verifies old-worker and registered-frontend exit, one exact old-lease release and canonical lock acquisition before the new worker started. No foreign process was signaled and no lock file was deleted.</p><p>The new worker then stopped at its startup gate with zero scientific fit attempts, zero new forecasts and zero new metrics. The <a href="b063r5.html">earlier R4 failure and R5 preparation report</a> remains as a dated historical record.</p></aside>
<section id="r6-failure"><h2>Two distinct outcomes in the actual return</h2><div class="grid"><article class="panel"><h3>The portable process interface worked</h3><p>The owner used CPython 3.12.15 with both Python pidfd bindings absent. Typed <code>libc.pidfd_open</code> and <code>libc.pidfd_send_signal</code> successfully exercised the kernel interface. Recovery took <strong>79.452 seconds</strong>, with identity checks and preserved evidence.</p><p class="muted">This supersedes the earlier unknown-shutdown status for that exact old execution at the recorded recovery completion. Every future launch still checks current identity and ownership.</p></article><article class="panel"><h3>A test cleanup error blocked the worker</h3><p>The next gate passed <strong>115 of 116 unique cases</strong>. One missing-binding test produced three errors while cleaning up temporary module attributes that were already absent. The owner then returned <code>B032_FRESH_PACKAGE_TESTS_FAILED</code>.</p><p class="muted">These are test-fixture errors. The process-control adapter had already completed recovery; no scientific fit was attempted or failed.</p></article></div><details id="r6-clocks"><summary>Inspect actual timing and evidence scope</summary><p>The worker ran from <time datetime="2026-11-13T02:23:24.787845+00:00">02:23:24.788 UTC</time> to <time datetime="2026-11-13T02:24:13.231026+00:00">02:24:13.231 UTC on November 13</time>, approximately 6:23–6:24 p.m. Pacific on November 12. Its reported elapsed time was <strong>48.861 seconds</strong> and excludes the preceding recovery.</p><p>The return was then persisted and read back. Its instance-wall estimate was <strong>$0.03485</strong> for the worker interval, using the verified $2.57/hour rate. This excludes prelaunch recovery and is neither a bill nor exclusive project-cost attribution.</p></details></section>
<section id="r6-runtime"><h2>Measured progress and the next bottleneck</h2><div class="grid"><article class="panel"><h3>The independent observer kept its cadence</h3><p>Five actual owner observations were exported with intervals of <strong>10.000418, 10.000082, 10.000093 and 10.000080 seconds</strong>. The observed prefix contains the recovery report and runtime evidence needed for this review.</p><p class="muted">The owner CPU peak reported by the application ledger was 0.691 core equivalents, with zero scientific workers. A functioning watchdog does not establish twelve-core scientific throughput.</p></article><article class="panel"><h3>Native preflight consumed 44.908 seconds</h3><p>All <strong>26 synthetic serialization contracts</strong> passed across ten model families. None were reused across processes. The critical startup test gate then ran for only <strong>0.700 seconds</strong> and stopped the worker.</p><p class="muted">Pre-science data-store heartbeats recorded zero historical S3 GETs. The owner never reached data or model-cache consumption, so this is not a successful historical cache-rerun benchmark.</p></article></div></section>
<section id="r6-repair"><h2>The next executable repair</h2><div class="grid"><article class="panel"><h3>Portable test fixtures and early checks</h3><p>Tests preserve the exact original module state whether a binding was present or absent, and avoid simulated process identities that can collide with the real parent. Critical startup checks run before expensive native imports so a fixture failure stops promptly.</p></article><article class="panel"><h3>Authenticated native-validation reuse</h3><p>Persist bounded native-validation evidence under exact implementation, recipe and runtime identity. Reuse only matching verified evidence; a changed or invalid environment must not inherit approval.</p><p>Saved validation does not authorize model loading, change scientific identity, or count as a new fit.</p></article></div><details id="r6-engineering"><summary>Inspect validation and the prepared source fingerprint</summary><p id="r6-tests">__B063R6_TESTS__</p><p>Prepared B063R6 source fingerprint: <code id="r6-source">__B063R6_SOURCE__</code>.</p><p>The executable's preparation tests receive zero scientific-fit credit. R6 owner execution and measured scientific throughput remain pending.</p></details></section>
<section id="r6-remaining"><h2>Preserved science and remaining acceptance</h2><p>All 134 embedded content objects were reverified and retain the 22 prior R3 target fits. Existing games, model comparisons, original issue clocks, negative results and provider evidence remain preserved. This run introduces no new champion promotion.</p><ol><li>Resume compatible durable work after the repaired startup gates pass.</li><li>Measure actual simultaneous scientific fits and throughput across all 12 safely available project cores.</li><li>Refresh every eligible current-season and upcoming game, with original issue clocks and actual outcomes.</li><li>Reevaluate former, current and rolling champions on the required seasons and all seven metrics, using genuine time-matched DraftKings, Kalshi and Polymarket data.</li></ol><div class="links"><a class="primary" href="index.html">Open preserved NCAA dashboard</a><a href="b063r5.html">Inspect the previous incident</a><a id="r6-download" href="data/B063R6_PUBLIC_STATUS.json" download>Download exact status JSON</a></div></section>
